---
title: Substitution cipher
tags: tools
---
{% from "macros/tool.njk" import toolSection with context %}
{% from "macros/tool-frame.njk" import toolFrame %}
{% set filename = page.fileSlug %}
{% set intro %}
<p class="px-2">
    A substitution cipher uses a key or a phrase to make a new alphabet, with the end result potentially being a completely jumbled up alphabet. 
</p>
<p class="px-2">
    A quick example substitution: 
    <code class="d-inline-flex px-2 bg-success bg-opacity-10 border border-success border-opacity-10 rounded-2">
        WORLD
    </code> &srarr; 
    <code class="d-inline-flex px-2 bg-success bg-opacity-10 border border-success border-opacity-10 rounded-2">
        HELLO
    </code>
    &srarr; 
    <code class="d-inline-flex px-2 bg-success bg-opacity-10 border border-success border-opacity-10 rounded-2">
        WNRJO
    </code> 
    - The full alphabet would look like 
    <code class="d-inline-flex px-2 bg-success bg-opacity-10 border border-success border-opacity-10 rounded-2">
        HELOABCDFGIJKMNPQRSTUVWXYZ
    </code> &ndash; notice that H, E, L and O have moved to the start, the second L in HELLO isn't present again as it has already been used and placed. 
    The case of your text is kept, and the key's case doesn't matter, for example:
    <code class="d-inline-flex px-2 bg-success bg-opacity-10 border border-success border-opacity-10 rounded-2">
        WOrld
    </code> &srarr;
    <code class="d-inline-flex px-2 bg-success bg-opacity-10 border border-success border-opacity-10 rounded-2">
        HEllo
    </code>
    &srarr;
    <code class="d-inline-flex px-2 bg-success bg-opacity-10 border border-success border-opacity-10 rounded-2">
        WNrjo
    </code> &ndash; There is more information available on the <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Substitution_cipher" class="text-convrtr">Substitution cipher</a> Wikipedia page. 
</p>
{% endset %}
{% call toolSection(intro) %}
{% call toolFrame(filename, "Substitution cipher", placeholder = "Example: Hello &srarr; World [key] &srarr; Cdhhk") %}
<div class="input-group w-auto">
    <label class="input-group-text" for="{{ filename }}Key"><span class="visually-hidden">Substitution </span>Key</label>
    <input type="text" class="form-control" id="{{ filename }}Key" autocomplete="off" aria-describedby="{{ filename }}Status">
    <button class="btn btn-convrtr" type="button" id="{{ filename }}Encrypt">Encrypt</button>
</div>
{% endcall %}
{% endcall %}
